.TH "ROARK\-CALL\-TOOL\-INVOCATION\-APPEND" "1" "" "roark-call-tool-invocation-append" "Roark Analytics API Manual"
.SH "NAME"
roark\-call\-tool\-invocation\-append \- Append tool invocations to a call
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B roark call tool\-invocation append
\fIcall\-id\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Attach tool invocations that fired during a call to an already\-existing call, asynchronously after the call was created. Use this when the tool\-call data becomes available later than the call itself (e.g. a Roark simulation, or a call submitted via POST /v1/call before its tools were ready). Writes are idempotent: re\-sending an invocation already present on the call (same tool name and timing) is skipped, so retries converge instead of double\-counting. Optionally pass `metrics` to (re)score metrics over the newly attached tools, which triggers a billed metric collection job and requires the `metric:create` permission.
.SH "API"
POST /v1/call/{callId}/tool\-invocations
.SH "ARGUMENTS"
.TP
\fIcall\-id\fR
The call\-id.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-tool\-invocations\fR \fI<value>\fR
Tool invocations that fired during the call, to attach to it. Max 500 per request. Re\-sending an invocation already present on the call (same tool name and timing) is skipped, so retries are safe. Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-metrics\fR \fI<value>\fR
Optional. Metric definitions to (re)score on this call after the tool invocations are attached, e.g. the Tool Invocation Analysis metrics. Triggers a metric collection job (billed, credit\-gated) and requires the 'metric:create' permission. Omit to attach tools without scoring. Max 20. Optional.
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-data\fR \fI<json>\fR
Request body as JSON, or @file to read one (@\- for stdin).
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip confirmation prompts.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-input\fR
Never prompt; fail instead.
.TP
\fB\-\-base\-url\fR \fI<url>\fR
API base URL.
.TP
\fB\-\-token\fR \fI<token>\fR
Bearer token. Prefer ROARK_API_BEARER_TOKEN or the stored credential.
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fI<ms>\fR
Request timeout in milliseconds.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-retries\fR \fI<count>\fR
Retries for retryable failures.
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<format>\fR
Output format: auto, json, jsonl, plain.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Shorthand for \-\-format json.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Disable colour.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress non\-essential output.
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-project\-base\-url\fR
Send the stored credential to a base URL set by a project .roark.json. Refused by default.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
roark call tool\-invocation append <call\-id> \-\-tool\-invocations <value>
.fi
